{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"J2 HELD-OUT VALIDATION (Phase 4e) -> ALL GREEN, first pass, no re-dispatch needed.\n\nTIERING: implementer dispatched as a STANDARD/mid-tier subagent (sonnet), explicitly named on dispatch (not inherited). Rationale: a multi-file refactor implemented against a test-pinned spec — not transcription-level, so cheap tier was not warranted; not novel design, so strong tier was not needed. Result: 46/46 green on the first validation, ZERO escalations. The brief carried the constraints the behavioral oracle cannot see (800-LOC hard cap from .github/module-size-limit.txt, ruff lint/format, and the aliased-import technique that makes the 'acli*.py import-lines-only' AC satisfiable at all).\n\nVALIDATION: 46 passed — 21 happy-path (the only file it saw) + 25 HELD-OUT tests it never saw (17 structural boundary + 8 ACLI behavioral). It satisfied behavior and contracts it could not read.\n\nCONSTRAINT ACs VERIFIED BY DIFF (not by assertion):\n - J1's oracle: EXACTLY ONE line changed, an import (_RELATION_TO_JIRA_LINK re-pointed to the public jira_family name, bound to the same local alias). ZERO assertions touched. Its classify_probe_response and RESOLVED_STATUS_NAMES imports still resolve as-is, exactly as the recorded execution decision required.\n - acli.py / acli_cli_ops.py / acli_graph.py: 'git diff -U0' shows import lines ONLY. __all__ lists and every call site byte-identical, achieved via aliased imports as briefed.\n - _loader.py untouched; zero renames; all three location-pinned modules still at their pinned paths.\n\nMUTATION / TEETH (3 perturbations, each reverted):\n 1. deleted->Done changed to deleted->Archived  => held-out ACLI test RED (correct test, correct reason).\n 2. added 'from rebar_reconciler.adapters.jira.adf import ...' into jira_family/sanitizers.py => BOTH boundary graph tests RED, naming the offending file.\n 3. re-added a _LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA binding in jira_fields.py (the exact shim the AC forbids) => no-shim test RED.\n Restored => 46/46 green again. No tautologies.\n\nREFACTORING LITMUS: renamed jira_family/value_maps.py -> maps.py and rewired its imports (behavior-preserving). All 46 still passed, so the oracle asserts observable behavior and the package's public contract, not internal file structure. Restored the original layout.\n\nSHAPE OF THE RESULT: adapters/jira_family/ = __init__.py 63, identity.py 36, probe.py 49, sanitizers.py 149, value_maps.py 72 (369 LOC total, every file far under the 800 cap).\n\nPRE-FLIGHT (Phase 4f): make lint GREEN after I fixed TWO E501 long lines in MY OWN held-out test file (my defect, not the implementer's); make typecheck GREEN (mypy, 385 source files, no issues — up from 381, the new package). Full suite 'pytest -m not integration and not external' running now."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785343132814261001,"uuid":"73d79c70-f46e-4182-80e3-0406fb540f6a"}